      "title": "Angus Taylor vows biggest cut to migration in Australia’s history, slashing 650,000 temporary visas",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/06/coalition-immigration-policy-angus-taylor-one-nation-labor-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Opposition leader says Coalition would reduce net overseas migration to 100,000 for two years </p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Angus Taylor says a Coalition government would cut net overseas migration to 100,000 for two years, calling the plan “the biggest cut to immigration in the history” of Australia.</p><p>Following moves by One Nation and Labor to capitalise on growing anti-migration sentiment, the opposition leader announced plans by the Liberals and Nationals on Tuesday, promising net overseas migration rates of 130,000 in the third year and 160,000 in the fourth.</p><p>tougher screening of visa applicants;</p><p>revising the temporary skilled priority list;</p><p>establishing a strike force to clear the backlog of skilled construction applications to address workforce shortages;</p><p>doubling the talent and innovation allocation to 7,000 places, through a new Aukus and Five Eyes visa;</p><p>linking each student visa to the enrolling institution;</p><p>introducing a new Agriculture Visa from 2030</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/06/coalition-immigration-policy-angus-taylor-one-nation-labor-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-06T03:17:57"
    },
    {
      "title": "Beau Lamarre-Condon trial shown CCTV of accused’s movements across Sydney after alleged double murder",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-cctv-accuseds-movements-sydney-after-alleged-double-murder-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Former NSW police officer has pleaded not guilty to February 2024 murders of Jesse Baird, 26, and Luke Davies, 29</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Jurors have seen how dozens of CCTV cameras tracked Beau Lamarre-Condon’s movements across Sydney well into the night after he allegedly murdered his former partner.</p><p>The 31-year-old former senior constable has pleaded not guilty to the murders of Jesse Baird and the 26-year-old’s new partner, Luke Davies, saying they were killed in two separate violent struggles.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/06/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-cctv-accuseds-movements-sydney-after-alleged-double-murder-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
